// Cloudflare's deploy tool, Wrangler, reads this on every build.
//
// Without it, every build GUESSED which folder to publish. The first build log
// says so: "Detected Project Settings: Framework: Static, Output Directory:
// dist". It guessed right — and a guess made fresh on each deploy is one
// detection change away from publishing the repository root, DECISIONS.md and
// the tests included, while still reporting success.
//
// dist/ is what `npm run ci` builds: the 40 files the game loads, and nothing
// else (scripts/build-site.js). tests/build.test.js fails if this ever points
// somewhere else, and if a `main` script appears — that would be a backend,
// which has its own plan.
//
// Full-line comments only, so the test can read it as plain JSON.
{
  "name": "g-ads-simulation",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-11",
  "workers_dev": true,
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist"
  }
}
